After dinner, I tidy up the kitchen.
Then I go into the living room.
I sit on the sofa and relax.
I take my mobile phone.
I call my family in Mexico.
In Berlin, it is evening now.
But in Mexico, it is only afternoon.
My younger sister Sofia answers.
"Hello Maya!" says Sofia.
"Hello Sofia, how are you?" I ask.
"I am very well," she says.
We talk about my day.
Suddenly, I hear a noise.
Our family dog Lola comes into the room.
Lola sees me on the screen.
She barks loudly at the camera.
I laugh.
"Hello Lola!" I say.
Sofia laughs too.
I am always happy about these calls.
